New features are scoped **per session** with the operator — not from a stale phase doc.

## Stack (verified — do not re-discover)

- Next.js 15 App Router + React 19 + TypeScript strict.
- Supabase Postgres + Storage + Auth; `@supabase/ssr`.
- Server: `src/lib/supabase-server.ts` (`createSupabaseServerClient`, `createSupabaseRouteHandlerClient` for route handlers that redirect).
- Browser: `src/lib/supabase-browser.ts`.
- Player auth: Supabase only. Admin auth: HMAC cookie in `src/lib/app-signing.ts` — **do not refactor admin auth** unless explicitly asked.
- Stripe `^20`, DocuSeal waivers, Tailwind, in-repo components.
- World Cup slug-gated pricing: `src/lib/world-cup-pricing.ts` (`world-cup-summer-tournament`).
- No new npm packages without operator approval.

## Conventions for new work

- **Scope:** Smallest correct diff. Match existing patterns. Log surprises in `FOLLOWUPS.md` (`- [topic] … — discovered YYYY-MM-DD`).
- **Migrations:** `supabase/migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_name.sql` only; include rollback in a comment; never destructive without explicit yes.
- **Player routes:** `getCurrentPlayer()`, `supabase.auth.getUser()` (not `getSession()`).
- **Admin routes:** `verifyAdmin` / `verifyAdminSessionCookieValue`; pages use `AdminGate`.
- **Auth route handlers:** Bind cookies to the outgoing `NextResponse` (see `/auth/callback`).
- **TypeScript:** Strict; no `any` at API boundaries.
- **No emojis** in code, comments, or UI copy.

## What not to redo without a regression report

- Full player auth surface (Phases 9–15).
- World Cup pay/register paths unless slug `world-cup-summer-tournament`.
- Admin `drop_ins` tool (guest play per round — separate from any future “open play” product idea).

## Deferred idea (not built)

A past roadmap proposed **open-play** single-day events (`event_type` on `tournaments`,
simplified register, public roster). **None of that exists in the repo.** Do not
start it unless the operator defines a new scoped project.
